  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "V3JAHwIAoYptfImydXlgtK9X1G4=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:35:10.000Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "`DocumentToolbar` does not lay its controls out as one flat row. `defaultControlSlots` in `packages/design-system/src/connect/components/document-toolbar/constants.ts` splits them into three named groups, and `ControlSlot` is the literal union `\"first\" | \"second\" | \"third\"`:\n\n```ts\nexport const defaultControlSlots = {\n  first: [\"undo\", \"redo\", \"download\"],   // primary document actions\n  second: [\"name\"],                       // document identity\n  third: [\"update\", \"history\", \"switchboard\", \"close\"], // secondary actions\n} as const;\n```\n\nThe slot names are the addressing scheme for `customControls` \u2014 you target a group, never an index \u2014 and `documentToolbarControls` (the source of the `DocumentToolbarControlName` union that `enabledControls` / `disabledControls` accept) is derived by spreading the three slots in order, so slot membership also fixes render order.\n\n**The eighth control.** Source has **eight** built-in controls, not seven. The `third` slot leads with `update`, mapped in `defaultControlComponents` to `ToolbarUpgradeButton`. The academy page (`00-DocumentToolbar.mdx`) lists only `[\"undo\", \"redo\", \"download\", \"name\", \"history\", \"switchboard\", \"close\"]` and shows `third` as `[\"history\", \"switchboard\", \"close\"]` \u2014 the doc has not been updated for the upgrade control, so treat source as authoritative here.\n\n`ToolbarUpgradeButton` is conditional rather than always-on, which is presumably why it went unnoticed: it calls `useDocumentVersionStatus(document)` and returns `null` unless the status is `\"upgrade-available\"` **and** `canUpgrade` is true. When it does render, it shows an `Update available` label and its click handler fires `showPHModal({ type: \"confirmDocumentUpgrade\", documentId })`.\n\nOne rough edge: unlike every other built-in button, `ToolbarUpgradeButton` is **not** re-exported from the component's `index.ts`. So `update` is overridable through `componentOverrides` but the default implementation cannot be imported and wrapped the way `ToolbarDownloadButton` can.\n\n_Source: packages/design-system/src/connect/components/document-toolbar/{constants.ts,types.ts,toolbar-button.tsx,index.ts}, cross-checked against apps/academy/docs/academy/03-Build/03-BuildingUserExperiences/06-DocumentTools/00-DocumentToolbar.mdx (Powerhouse v6.2.2-dev.45)._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-14T12:35:10.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:35:10.000Z"
    }
  },
